      en: "Umma (modern Tell Jokha) was a Sumerian city-state in southern Iraq, known for its long-standing rivalry with neighboring Lagash. This conflict is famously depicted on the 'Stele of the Vultures' (c. 2450 BC), which shows the victory of Lagash over Umma. The city was dedicated to the god Shara and was a major center for agriculture and trade, controlling fertile lands along the Tigris-Euphrates basin. Umma flourished during the Early Dynastic III period and later under the Akkadian Empire. Archaeological excavations have uncovered large archives of cuneiform tablets detailing temple administration, land management, and labor allocation. The site covers about 150 hectares and includes a ziggurat and palace complex. Umma declined after the Ur III period but remained inhabited until the Kassite era.",
