      en: "The Fortress of Al-Raheb (Qaṣr al-Rāhib) is a medieval castle in Al-Anbar province, western Iraq, located in the desert near the town of Hit. Likely built during the Abbasid period, it served as a caravanserai and military outpost to protect trade routes crossing the Syrian Desert. The rectangular structure features thick walls and corner towers. It fell into disrepair after the Mongol invasions. In 2015, the Islamic State damaged the site. Surviving elements include vaulted halls and arrow slits.",
